  "native_semantics": [
    "value subqueries require an aggregate function as their column or LIMIT 1 (mx check CE0174); a grouped aggregate fails at run time with several rows",
    "NOT IN over candidates containing NULL selects nothing; IN, EXISTS and joins compare text case-insensitively",
    "subqueries may be correlated, nested and used in HAVING and projections; with LIMIT they may order by unprojected source columns",
    "UNION removes duplicates ignoring case and keeps the first spelling; UNION ALL keeps all rows; columns take the first part names",
    "views may read other views in FROM and joins, in chains",
    "ANY, ALL, BETWEEN and SELECT * are rejected by Mendix; Count is a reserved word"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "dataset parameters and UNION in tabular datasets remain unsupported",
    "a view that reads itself is rejected instead of looping"
